Attribution & clean-room boundary statement (ADR-004 discipline)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NovaLab is an original work. Where prior art informed its design, the
boundary below states exactly what was referenced and what was NOT copied.
"Clean-room" here means: ideas, semantics and interaction concepts were
studied from public documentation, published descriptions or screenshots,
and the implementation (code, tests, wording of assertions, visual assets)
was written from scratch by this project. No source code, stylesheet,
icon, font glyph or other expressive asset was copied from any reference
project into this repository.

1. Reactive execution semantics (py/novakernel, bridge DAG routing)
   - Referenced: marimo 0.25.1 (Apache-2.0) — the general approach of
     reactive notebook execution: AST-based definition/reference
     extraction, single-assignment DAG, staleness propagation,
     multiple-definition-as-compile-error, cycle detection.
   - NOT copied: no marimo source code, no vendored marimo files. The
     kernel (dag.py / runtime.py / introspect.py / serialize.py /
     server.py) is an independent implementation of these ideas against
     our own JSON-RPC protocol (docs/spec.md §5/§6). marimo is only
     present in the gitignored, read-only refs/ directory for study and
     is not part of the build or dependency graph. The bidirectional
     .py converter (py/novakernel/convert.py) reads and writes marimo's
     publicly documented `@app.cell` file format; implementing a format
     converter does not incorporate marimo code.

2. File browser interaction paradigm (app sidebar / file tree)
   - Referenced: JupyterLab (BSD-3-Clause) — the interaction model of its
     filebrowser package: tree navigation, create/rename/delete with
     confirmation, workspace-root scoping.
   - NOT copied: no JupyterLab source code or UI assets. Our components,
     handlers and tests were written from the described behavior alone.

3. UI visual design (dark, minimal, monospace design tokens; layout)
   - Referenced: publicly circulated screenshots of Claude Science
     Notebook — clean-room re-creation of layout and interaction
     elements (kernel tabs, live pill, cell header badges, collapsible
     output, status bar, inline REPL, session modal) as inventoried in
     docs/intent.md §4.
   - NOT copied: no pixel sampling, no extracted assets, no reverse
     engineering of any closed-source product. All design tokens, CSS
     and components are original. The name "NovaLab" deliberately avoids
     any third-party trademark; no affiliation with or endorsement by
     Anthropic is claimed or implied.

4. Fonts
